// T6 — A document version becomes design, section by section
//
// STORY FLOW (founder ruling bd996f3e, 2026-11-07, "15 story flows, branches inside"): the main path runs from the start of the thread to its T6.O6 terminal, in the order the spec tells it.
// Every alternative of the thread, once a flow of its own, is a branch at the moment where it diverges: a [branch] moment that holds its deciding event as a plain node (moved from the main path, not copied), an empty first arm `TheMainPath` (the walk takes the first arm when none is chosen, so the main path is the one that goes on after the moment) and one `when` arm for each alternative,
// each ending at its own exit ([outcome] when it is a normal outcome of the thread, [terminal] for a failure or a refusal) or falling through into the moments that follow. Moment derives one scenario for each path. A refusal is a precondition of a command; Moment 0.9.0 derives its negative scenario for every path of the flow (ADR-042). A branch moment that nothing precedes (the first node of the flow, or one whose deciding event is the only node of the previous branch moment's main arm) keeps its first arm `TheMainPath` with the main path's next nodes: no event to anchor on (docs/sidd/round30/story-flows-log.md, 0.9.0 rework).
// A branch arm cites the former flow it carries in its first comment line (the old-to-new mapping is in docs/sidd/round30/story-flows-log.md).
// BRANCHES:
//   T6.M2 · The bytes are taken in: ARedoRecordsTheContentHashOfADocumentVersionWhoseReceiptHasNone (former flow t6-a-redo-records-the-content-hash-of-a-document-version.moment)
//   T6.M2 · The bytes are taken in: TheLocationCannotBeRead (former flow t6-the-location-cannot-be-read.moment)
//   T6.M4 · The sections are placed, one at a time: TheDocumentCannotBeParsed (former flow t6-the-document-cannot-be-parsed.moment)
//   T6.M4 · The sections are placed, one at a time (continued): ASectionFailsAndStaysOpen (former flow t6-a-section-fails-and-stays-open.moment)
//   T6.M5 · The version closes (continued): ADocumentVersionThatStatesTheOwnerOfATermMovesTheTerm (former flow t6-a-document-version-that-states-the-owner-of-a-term-moves-the-term.moment)
//   T6.M6 · The release pass declares the verdict, and the questions arrive together: AStepAfterTheCloseFails (former flow t6-a-step-after-the-close-fails.moment)
//   T6.M6 · The release pass declares the verdict, and the questions arrive together: TheDocumentPassAsksTheREC001QuestionsOnTheDocumentVersion (former flow t6-the-document-pass-asks-the-rec-001-questions.moment)
// Part of the model directory; validate with `moment parse model/` (project mode) and `moment test` on this file.

flow "T6 — A document version becomes design, section by section"
  description "T6 — A document version becomes design, section by section. The story of the thread from its start to its T6.O6 outcome, with its alternatives as branches at the moment where each diverges. Source of record: docs/sidd/round30/pass7-domain-spec.md."

  lane intake "Intake" [Core]
  lane design "DesignModel" [Core]
  lane clarification "Clarification" [Core]

  moment "T6.M2 · The bytes are taken in" [branch]
    // [person] an operator (or the UI layer on their behalf) sends IntakeDocument(location, documentId, version) with a request key (external: narrative)
    // [oauth] management API (OAuth2, clientId); the intake ordinal is derived, not an input (S:390)
    intake: IntakeDocument  // S:390 "IntakeDocument(location, documentId, version), issued by whoever placed the document, through the management API"; S:285

    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story: no node here, the deciding event is the plain node above; the main path goes on in the moment that follows (founder ruling "Yes, anchor the branches": the deciding event is moved into the branch moment, the arm carries none of the main path's nodes)
    when ARedoRecordsTheContentHashOfADocumentVersionWhoseReceiptHasNone
      // former flow: t6-a-redo-records-the-content-hash-of-a-document-version.moment
      // T6.M2 · The document version is taken in again and the hash is recorded
      intake: RecordReceipt  // S:394 "RecordReceipt(Pointer (documentId, version, intake ordinal), Arrival Document(documentVersion)"
      intake: ContentHashRecorded [outcome]  // S:331 "by ContentHashRecorded when the Receipt exists without one"
    when TheLocationCannotBeRead
      // former flow: t6-the-location-cannot-be-read.moment
      // T6.M2·B3 · when the location cannot be read
      // T6.N3 · Intake open (terminal): the failed attempt is recorded on the document version's Receipt, with an Arrival that carries the location and no content hash (S:391); the verdict counts the intake as open.
      // RecordFailedAttempt is create-if-absent, so a Receipt exists although the read failed before RecordReceipt (S:332, S:345); a failed read records no content hash (S:394).
      intake: RecordFailedAttempt  // S:391 "step 1 (a location that cannot be read) ... RecordFailedAttempt, create-if-absent"; S:345
      intake: ReceiptRecorded  // S:332 "When the Receipt is absent, it records ReceiptRecorded{Arrival} first"
      intake: AttemptFailed [terminal]  // S:323 "AttemptFailed {cycleId, attempt, quarantined}"
      // The redo: the next IntakeDocument of the version, the tick (P1.06) or RedriveCycle (T9).

  moment "T6.M2 · The bytes are taken in (main path)"
    // the main path of the story
    // [doclocation] SG.DocumentIntake.1: read the bytes at the location and hash them (crossing: document location; S:394). Not declarable: the read and the content hash are steps of the IntakeDocument Cycle.
    intake: RecordReceipt  // S:394 "RecordReceipt(Pointer (documentId, version, intake ordinal), Arrival Document(documentVersion)"; S:316
    // ContentHashRecorded is the redo's event (a Receipt that exists without a hash, S:331, S:394), not the first intake's; it is not on this path.

  moment "T6.M3 · It is parsed and split"
    note intake: "SG.DocumentIntake.2: Markdown or plain text become sections in reading order, one per heading plus one preamble, flat, a leading byte-order mark ignored and a heading inside fenced code not a split, each with its heading path and SectionFingerprint; each section is held under its own data key and the raw bytes are discarded; a section longer than the input budget is split or refused with a reason code, never cut"  // S:395 "Markdown and plain text become **sections** in reading order, one per heading and one preamble for any text before the first heading"

  moment "T6.M4 · The sections are placed, one at a time" [branch]
    intake: ReceiptRecorded  // S:321 "ReceiptRecorded {Arrival}"; S:394
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story: no node here, the deciding event is the plain node above; the main path goes on in the moment that follows (founder ruling "Yes, anchor the branches": the deciding event is moved into the branch moment, the arm carries none of the main path's nodes)
    when TheDocumentCannotBeParsed
      // former flow: t6-the-document-cannot-be-parsed.moment
      // T6.M3·B1 · when the format is not Markdown or plain text, or the bytes are not text
      // T6.N3 · Intake open (terminal): a parse failure ends the unit of work Failed with the format's reason code and is recorded on the document version's Receipt; the raw bytes stay held, under the data key of the document version, for the redo (S:395).
      intake: RecordFailedAttempt  // S:395 "A parse failure ends the unit of work Failed with the format's reason code"; S:391
      intake: AttemptFailed [terminal]  // S:323
      // The format's reason code is not named by the spec (S:395 "with the format's reason code"; document-format ADR); no code is minted.

  moment "T6.M4 · The sections are placed, one at a time (main path)"
    // the main path of the story
    // SG.DocumentIntake.3 (S:396): the sections are dispatched in order, one at a time, each as a child Cycle; no model-wide pass starts inside the intake (S:339, S:396).
    intake: RecordReceipt  // S:396 "each as a child Cycle with RecordReceipt(the section's Pointer, Arrival Document(documentVersion))"

  moment "T6.M4 · The sections are placed, one at a time (continued)" [branch]
    intake: ReceiptRecorded  // S:321; S:396
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story: no node here, the deciding event is the plain node above; the main path goes on in the moment that follows (founder ruling "Yes, anchor the branches": the deciding event is moved into the branch moment, the arm carries none of the main path's nodes)
    when ASectionFailsAndStaysOpen
      // former flow: t6-a-section-fails-and-stays-open.moment
      // T6.M4·B1 · when a section fails
      // T6.N4 · A section failed and open (terminal): the section follows the entry-failure rule (redone by the next IntakeDocument or the tick, quarantined at the bound; S:396);
      // when every section is dispatched and one is failed and open, no close is recorded and the unit ends Failed and records NO attempt on the version's Receipt, because the section has its own bound (S:333, S:396).
      // That absence is not assertable by a node; the node below is the section's own failed attempt.
      intake: RecordFailedAttempt  // S:345 "RecordFailedAttempt ... when an entry's processing fails ... Replay children included"; S:396
      intake: AttemptFailed [terminal]  // S:323
      // T9.M1·B1 (a failure that is only a section still failed and open records no attempt on the version's Receipt) is this flow's note: S:333.

  moment "T6.M4 · The sections are placed, one at a time (continued, main path)"
    // the main path of the story
    // Extraction on the section text issues MatchCandidate once per candidate (S:373); status Proposed / Accepted / Superseded / unstated decides whether it is a deciding entry.
    design: MatchCandidate  // S:373 "Extraction ... issues MatchCandidate(Pointer, Fingerprint, Arrival) once per candidate the entry yields"
    design: CandidateMatched  // S:435 "CandidateMatched {Fingerprint}"
    // Placement and the gates are as T3 (S:396 "Extraction on the section's text, then Placement and the gates, unchanged"); a Steer a section raises is gathered, not posted (S:396).
    intake: MarkProcessed  // S:373 "then MarkProcessed (effect Applied ...)"; S:344
    intake: ReceiptProcessed  // S:322 "ReceiptProcessed {effect: Applied | None(reason)}"

  moment "T6.M5 · The version closes (continued)" [branch]
    // SG.DocumentIntake.4 (S:397): when every section's Receipt is processed, quarantined or closed, DocumentVersionProcessed {documentVersion, sections, upTo} is recorded,
    // one close per version.
    // The policies of DocumentVersionProcessed run in order (S:1350): StartPass(Document) first, started and not awaited, never SystemValidated; then, each only when its
    // condition holds, owner-keeping MoveConstruct(Computed) (S:641: flow t6-a-document-version-that-states-the-owner-of-a-term-moves-the-term), the REC-001 questions, the version-retirement AskQuestion
    // (S:521: flow t5-a-version-retirement-question-is-answered), its withdrawal, and the question sweep (S:397).
    intake: DocumentVersionProcessed  // S:397 "IntakeDocument records DocumentVersionProcessed {documentVersion, sections, upTo} (the close of the document version"

    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story: no node here, the deciding event is the plain node above; the main path goes on in the moment that follows (founder ruling "Yes, anchor the branches": the deciding event is moved into the branch moment, the arm carries none of the main path's nodes)
    when ADocumentVersionThatStatesTheOwnerOfATermMovesTheTerm
      // former flow: t6-a-document-version-that-states-the-owner-of-a-term-moves-the-term.moment
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, T6.M4 · The sections are placed, one at a time: note intake: "Steps 1 to 3 of the document intake as in the main flow: the bytes are taken in, parsed and split, and each section is dispatched as a child Cycle; one section states which context owns a Term that another context restated, and its LAN-006 Gap was resolved by a resolver"  // S:641 "DocumentVersionProcessed of a document version that states the owner of a Term another context restated, whose LAN-006 Gap a resolver resolved"
      // T6.M5 · Owner keeping moves the Term
      design: OwnerKeepingMovesTerm  // S:641 "owner keeping (§3 Gap): DocumentVersionProcessed of a document version that states the owner of a Term another context restated"
        triggered-by DocumentVersionProcessed
      design: MoveConstruct cause Computed  // S:641 "MoveConstruct(the Term, the stated owner's context, cause: Computed, Pointer: the stated owner's section) for each such Term whose newest stated owner differs from its context of record"
        triggered-by OwnerKeepingMovesTerm
      design: ConstructMoved [outcome]  // S:618 "ConstructMoved {from, to, cause, Pointer}"
      // The Term whose newest stated owner is its context of record is not moved; the policy records kind system, and a repeat is a no-op by its ID derived from the DocumentVersionProcessed (S:641): the precondition NoOpRepeat of MoveConstruct for the cause Computed derives that scenario.

  moment "T6.M5 · The version closes (continued, main path)"
    // the main path of the story
    design: DocumentVersionProcessedStartsDocumentPass  // S:397 "StartPass(Document, scope: the constructs the document version's sections placed) first, started and not awaited"
      triggered-by DocumentVersionProcessed
    design: StartPass  // S:397 "StartPass(Document, scope: the constructs the document version's sections placed) first, started and not awaited"; S:668
      triggered-by DocumentVersionProcessedStartsDocumentPass

  moment "T6.M6 · The release pass declares the verdict, and the questions arrive together" [branch]
    design: PassStarted  // S:672 "PassStarted {startPosition, CorpusVersion, RulesVersion}"
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story: no node here, the deciding event is the plain node above; the main path goes on in the moment that follows (founder ruling "Yes, anchor the branches": the deciding event is moved into the branch moment, the arm carries none of the main path's nodes)
    when AStepAfterTheCloseFails
      // former flow: t6-a-step-after-the-close-fails.moment
      // T6.M6·B1 · when a step after the close fails
      // T6.N3 · Intake open (terminal): the document version's Receipt stays failed and open until the redo completes; the redo reaches every reaction the failed attempt did not and ends with a release pass of its own (S:397).
      intake: RecordFailedAttempt  // S:391 "step 4 at any point, before or after the close, the release pass included"; S:397 "A step after the close that fails leaves the document version's Receipt failed and open"
      intake: AttemptFailed [terminal]  // S:323
    when TheDocumentPassAsksTheREC001QuestionsOnTheDocumentVersion
      // former flow: t6-the-document-pass-asks-the-rec-001-questions.moment
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, T6.M5 · The version closes: intake: IntakeDocument  // S:390 "IntakeDocument(location, documentId, version), issued by whoever placed the document"
      // carried from the former flow, T6.M5 · The version closes: intake: DocumentVersionProcessed  // S:397 "IntakeDocument records DocumentVersionProcessed {documentVersion, sections, upTo}"
      // T6.M5·B2 · when the Document pass finds a REC-001 gap
      design: RecordGateResults  // S:669 "RecordGateResults(sequence number, evaluated constructs[], findings[])"
        triggered-by PassStarted  // S:720 "Gate run: PassStarted → GateRun" (policy PassStartedRunsGates)
      design: GapIdentified  // S:673 "GapIdentified {GapKey {rule, construct, origin}"
      design: ObserveGap  // S:721 "GapIdentified → ObserveGap"
        triggered-by GapIdentified  // S:721 "GapIdentified → ObserveGap" (policy GapIdentifiedObservesGap)
      design: GapOpened  // S:750 "GapOpened {handling, pass, finding, carriedFrom?}"
      design: DocumentPassRec001Questions  // S:1350 "the Document pass's REC-001 questions on the document version's subject"
        triggered-by DocumentVersionProcessed
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:809 "Ask → AskQuestion (subject: GapKey"
        triggered-by DocumentPassRec001Questions
      clarification: QuestionAsked [outcome]  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule, CorpusVersion, SubjectVersions shown?};"

  moment "T6.M6 · The release pass declares the verdict, and the questions arrive together (main path)"
    // the main path of the story
    // The intake ends with its release pass (S:397, S:732): StartPass(Convergence, model-wide), the last pass of the intake, after every policy of DocumentVersionProcessed.
    // It does not count the version's own Receipt and declares the verdict (S:397). Gate run and CompletePass between PassStarted and PassCompleted are as T10.M1 (S:720-723).
    design: StartPass  // S:732 "the end of an intake ... StartPass(Convergence, scope: the customer workspace, model-wide), the release pass"; S:397
      triggered-by DocumentVersionProcessed  // S:397 "run the policies of DocumentVersionProcessed in their listed order (§11.1): StartPass(Document, scope: the constructs the document version's sections placed) first" (policy DocumentVersionProcessedStartsDocumentPass)
    design: PassStarted  // S:672
    design: PassCompleted  // S:675 "PassCompleted {ConvergenceSnapshot, verdict, ...}"; S:397
    // The intake's one flush of the gathered postings (QPOST) follows the release pass (S:397); a poster side effect, not a command.
    intake: MarkProcessed  // S:397 "MarkProcessed on the document version's Receipt ends the intake"; S:344
    // What the version decided reaches flmnt as Sift pointers (T3.M7), not from the intake (S:397).

  moment "T6.O6 · A document version became design (terminal)"
    // PROVES: DocumentVersionProcessed (the close, M5), a release PassCompleted with the verdict (M6), ReceiptProcessed for the version; every section's Receipt processed, quarantined or closed (M4); Sift pointers for its decisions in flmnt (T3.M7).
    intake: ReceiptProcessed [terminal]  // S:322; S:397 "the document version's Receipt is processed once the redo completes"
    // T6.N3 Intake open: t6-the-location-cannot-be-read, t6-the-document-cannot-be-parsed, t6-a-step-after-the-close-fails; also the quarantined no-op arm of the refusal flow.
    // T6.N4 A section failed and open: t6-a-section-fails-and-stays-open.
